The '''Randon Run''' was a [[hyperspace route]] which ran between the<ref name="RO locations" /> [[planet]]<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|nix-jerd|Nix Jerd}}</ref> [[Lantillies]] and the astronomical object [[Randon]] in the [[Mid Rim Territories]]. From Lantillies, which was situated along the<ref name="Timelines">{{GalaxyMapPoster}}</ref> [[super-hyperroute]]<ref name="BMF 48">{{BuildFalconCite|48|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> known as the [[Perlemian Trade Route]],<ref name="Timelines" /> the Randon Run went south<ref name="RO locations" /> to the<ref name="Timelines" /> planet<ref name="Bracca DB">{{Databank|bracca|Bracca}}</ref> [[Bracca]] in the [[Bracca system]]. After Bracca, the route reached the<ref name="Timelines" /> planet<ref name="Aftermath">[[Aftermath (novel)|''Aftermath'']]</ref> [[Uyter]], which was linked by hyperlane to<ref name="Timelines" /> the [[Nazzri system|Nazzri]] and [[Togoria system]]s.<ref name="TFABG">[[Star Wars: The Force Awakens Beginner Game|''Star Wars: The Force Awakens'' Beginner Game]]</ref>

The Randon Run then went to the planet [[Kashyyyk]], in the [[Kashyyyk system]] of the [[Mytaranor sector]]. At Kashyyyk, the route was at a junction with the hyperspace routes known as the [[Durkteel Loop]], the [[Great Kashyyyk Branch]] and the [[Nightroad]].<ref name="Collapse" /> Following Kashyyyk, the Randon Run reached Randon, a junction with the [[Pabol Sleheyron]] hyperspace route.<ref name="RO locations" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Randon Run was first mentioned in the [[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon 43|forty-third issue]] of [[De Agostini]]'s magazine series ''[[Star Wars: Build the Millennium Falcon]]'',<ref name="BMF 43">{{BuildFalconCite|43|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> published on approximately [[October 28]], [[2015]].<ref name="BMFdate">{{BuildFalconDates|43}}</ref>

